Falsifies `entropy_contract::verification::a_fill_succeeds_exactly_when_every_reply_is_full`.

The defect: `fill_with` refuses only a reply that delivers more than it asked for, and accepts a
short one. The standard library's caller accepts partial counts on purpose; this function promises
the opposite, and the defect quietly leaves bytes in the slice that the service never sent.

Expected to fail: the harness's match on the result, which meets `Ok` where one reply was short.

--- a/crates/entropy_contract/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/entropy_contract/src/lib.rs
@@ -407,7 +407,7 @@
         let asked = (out.len() - filled).min(MAXIMUM_BYTES as usize);
         let (first_reply_word, reply_word) = call(request(GET, asked as u64));
         let delivered = delivered_bytes(first_reply_word).ok_or(Refusal::NoService)?;
-        if delivered != asked {
+        if delivered > asked {
             return Err(Refusal::ShortReply { asked, delivered });
         }
         filled += copy_delivered_bytes(asked, reply_word, &mut out[filled..]);
